# Vulnerability details

## Description

The ERC20Minimal contract lacks the implementation of the safeTransfer function, which introduces a security vulnerability when transferring tokens to contract addresses. This vulnerability is primarily observed in the `transfer` and `transferFrom` functions of the contract at `ERC20Minimal::transfer` `ERC20Minimal::transferFrom` `ERC20Minimal::_transferFrom`

The absence of safeTransfer means that there are no additional safety checks performed when transferring tokens to contract addresses. As a result, tokens can be sent to contracts that are not capable of handling them, potentially leading to token loss or unexpected behavior.

```
    function transfer(address to, uint256 amount) public virtual returns (bool) {
        balanceOf[msg.sender] -= amount;

        // Cannot overflow because the sum of all user
        // balances can't exceed the max uint256 value.
        unchecked {
            balanceOf[to] += amount;
        }

        emit Transfer(msg.sender, to, amount);

        return true;
    }
```

## Impact

The impact of this finding is significant, as it exposes users to the risk of token loss and potential security vulnerabilities. Without the safety checks provided by safeTransfer, tokens can be mistakenly sent to contracts that do not support the ERC-20 interface or handle token transfers incorrectly. Additionally, the contract also utilizes the `unchecked` keyword, which further exacerbates the risk of unintended behavior in token transfers.

