# Vulnerability details

A malicious user or MEV bot can steal funds from depositors by frontrunning and backrunning their `deposit` transaction. A bot can do this anytime it is profitable or simply to grieve a user.
This attack is profitable when the user wants to deposit more than 2x the total supply.

## Impact 

Loss of funds for the victim. The victim will have to pay more fees than earlier expected. They will also be minted less shares.

## Proof of Concept

The Liquidity Pool just got started and Alice wants to deposit 100^18 worth of tokens. A malicious user monitoring the memepool can see her transaction and front-run her in other to steal fees from her and previous depositors.

- Alice `deposit` 100^18 worth of tokens to the pool.
- Before her transaction is mined an Attacker `deposit` 100^18 tokens.
- The Attacker's transaction get mined first so he gains 0.5^18 tokens
- Alice Loses 0.5 ^ 18 tokens and get 999.5^18 tokens instead of 999^18


